# Phase 6C — the AWS Lambda migration made api/newsroom/** the ONLY
# authoritative Newsroom backend (aws/newsroom-lambda.ts imports these exact
# files as its business logic; the currently-deployed Lambda IS a bundled
# copy of this code). These files are NOT obsolete — deleting them would
# strand the Lambda's own build pipeline, since aws/router.ts's dynamic
# imports and every scripts/newsroom-*.ts test script still need them as
# real source. What they must NOT be is independently reachable as live
# Vercel serverless functions — that would stand up a second, parallel
# Newsroom backend (Browser -> Vercel -> RDS/S3 directly) alongside the
# intended one (Browser -> API Gateway -> Lambda -> RDS/S3), each requiring
# its own DB/AWS credentials and each capable of drifting from the other.
#
# This file excludes them from what `vercel deploy` uploads/routes, while
# leaving them on disk for local tooling (esbuild bundling the Lambda,
# `tsx` running the test scripts, `vercel dev` for local iteration) — all
# of which read the working tree directly and are unaffected by this file.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: api/newsroom-admin-proxy/** (the thin relay —
# the only Newsroom-related Vercel function meant to stay live) and
# api/_lib/** (Vercel's own convention already never routes an
# underscore-prefixed path as a function regardless of this file; excluding
# it here too would break api/newsroom-admin-proxy/*.ts's own imports of
# ../_lib/http and ../_lib/adminProxySession at Vercel's build time).
api/newsroom/

# Same reasoning as api/newsroom/ above, for the Phase 3 Projects backend:
# api/projects/** is the menasco-projects-api Lambda's own business logic
# (aws/projects-router.ts's dynamic imports point at these exact files) —
# not independently reachable as a live Vercel serverless function, which
# would stand up a second, parallel Projects backend with its own
# DB/AWS credentials capable of drifting from the real one
# (Browser -> API Gateway -> menasco-projects-api -> RDS/S3).
api/projects/

# *.test.ts files colocated under api/ (Vitest convention, e.g.
# api/newsroom-article-page.test.ts) are source, not routes — Vercel's
# zero-config function detection otherwise treats every api/**/*.ts file as
# a deployable Serverless Function, which would stand up a live, pointless
# /api/newsroom-article-page.test endpoint. Excluded from the deploy
# entirely (tests still run locally via `npm test`, which reads the working
# tree directly and is unaffected by this file).
api/**/*.test.ts
